messages.content:
Write an incident policy for the course-registration website our student club maintains (6 volunteer developers, 2 of them maintainers).
Rules: at most 4 rules; every rule must say who may trigger it; include one rule for database outages.

Reply with JSON only, in this shape: {"rules": [{"trigger": "...", "action": "...", "who_can_trigger": "..."}]}

output:
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "trigger": "A student reports that their registration form submission fails with a 500 error",
      "action": "One of the two maintainers must investigate the error logs and deploy a hotfix if a code bug is confirmed; the other volunteer developers must assist in testing the fix.",
      "who_can_trigger": "Any student or club member who observes the error"
    },
    {
      "trigger": "The website is unresponsive for more than 5 minutes during peak registration hours",
      "action": "The two maintainers must immediately check server health and restart the application container; if the issue persists, they must notify the club lead and initiate a backup server failover.",
      "who_can_trigger": "Any volunteer developer or club lead observing the website downtime"
    },
    {
      "trigger": "A database query takes longer than 3 seconds during a registration attempt",
      "action": "The maintainers must analyze the database query logs and optimize the query or index; the volunteer developers must monitor performance until resolved.",
      "who_can_trigger": "Any volunteer developer monitoring performance metrics"
    },
    {
      "trigger": "The database is unreachable or the website cannot connect to the database",
      "action": "The maintainers must switch to the backup database instance and notify the club lead; all registration functions must be paused until the primary database is restored.",
      "who_can_trigger": "Any volunteer developer or maintainer detecting database unavailability"
    }
  ]
}

